%
H:This is an old, traditional children's song in the version 
H:most often sung in the American South. 
H:Stories around its origin vary, but variants go back to the 1500's
H:in Scotland and it is often attributed as political satire 
H:around the proposed marriage between Queen Elizabeth and the French
H:ambassador (her "Frog"). 
H:http://dandutton.com/DanDuttonsBallad/froggy.html has excellent
H:information on the history of the song.
%
O:US Southern variant of 16th-century Scottish/British folk tune
%
N:This is based on the version printed in Best Loved Songs of the 
N:American People by Denes Agay, although I have selected the verses
N:and modified the lyrics to best match what my Appalachian
N:parents and grand-parents taught me as a child.
N:Plays well on harp and clarinet
